# 17.3 Folder Type Enumeration

KnowledgeOS uses a PostgreSQL ENUM to distinguish between different folder categories.

```sql
CREATE TYPE folder_type_enum AS ENUM (
    'uploaded',
    'quick_notes',
    'archive',
    'custom'
);
```

### Folder Types

| Folder Type | Description |
|-------------|-------------|
| uploaded | Default folder for uploaded documents |
| quick_notes | Stores notes created inside KnowledgeOS |
| archive | Stores archived documents that remain searchable |
| custom | User-created folders |

Using an ENUM instead of relying on folder names keeps backend logic independent of UI labels and supports future localization.

---

# 17.4 Table Schema

| Column | Data Type | Nullable | Default | Description |
|---------|-----------|----------|----------|-------------|
| id | UUID | No | gen_random_uuid() | Primary Key |
| profile_id | UUID | No | — | References profiles(id) |
| name | VARCHAR(100) | No | — | Folder display name |
| folder_type | folder_type_enum | No | 'custom' | Folder category |
| description | TEXT | Yes | NULL | Optional folder description |
| color | VARCHAR(20) | Yes | NULL | Future folder color label |
| icon | VARCHAR(50) | Yes | NULL | Future folder icon |
| is_system_folder | BOOLEAN | No | FALSE | Indicates application-managed folder |
| document_count | INTEGER | No | 0 | Cached number of active documents |
| created_at | TIMESTAMPTZ | No | NOW() | Creation timestamp |
| updated_at | TIMESTAMPTZ | No | NOW() | Last modification timestamp |

