# 17.7 Automatic System Folder Creation

Immediately after a new user profile is created, KnowledgeOS automatically creates three system folders.

```text
Uploaded

Quick Notes

Archive
```

Characteristics:

- Cannot be deleted
- Cannot change folder type
- Always exist
- Created automatically
- Hidden from folder creation limits

If a folder creation transaction fails, the entire onboarding transaction is rolled back to maintain consistency.

---

# 17.8 Folder Lifecycle

## Creating a Folder

Users may create unlimited custom folders.

Requirements:

- Unique name per user (recommended)
- folder_type = custom
- is_system_folder = FALSE

---

## Renaming a Folder

Only custom folders can be renamed.

System folders cannot be renamed in the MVP.

---

## Moving Documents

Documents may be moved freely between folders.

Moving a document updates:

- folder_id
- document_count (cached values)

No document content is modified.

---

## Archiving Documents

Moving a document into the Archive folder:

- Removes it from the main Uploaded view.
- Keeps embeddings active.
- Keeps the document searchable through AI.
- Keeps metadata unchanged.

Archived documents continue participating in semantic retrieval.

---

## Deleting a Folder

Only custom folders can be deleted.

Before deletion:

- Documents must either
  - Move to another folder selected by the user, or
  - Automatically move to Uploaded.

Deleting a folder never deletes its documents.

